# INERT. NOTHING READS THIS FILE. Do not add rules here (issue #608).
#
# This is Netlify / Cloudflare Pages syntax. We serve the site from a Bun
# process behind a cloudflared tunnel (backend/src/api/static.ts), and nothing
# in that path parses `_headers`. Cloudflare Pages Git integration, Transform
# Rules, and legacy Page Rules are all confirmed unused (issue #670; Cloudflare
# is DNS + observability only, docs/decisions.md D13/D29) — there is no live
# Pages project left to read this file, for production or otherwise.
#
# Kept rather than deleted only because it documents the intended header
# policy (same call PR #603 made for `frontend/prod/_redirects`). The real
# security headers live in `shellResponse()` in `backend/src/api/static.ts`.
# If this file ever starts reading as live config again, delete this notice.
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=300, must-revalidate
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN
